Evident creator

    - none of these in itself explains the coincidence
        - the null explanans certainly does not
        - of the remaining explanantia, all are given to be indeterminate
            : see `^*• .+explainable by a \(yet unknown\) theory` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : see `^*• .+cull of a \(yet unknown\) natural process` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : see `^*• .+bound.+by a \(yet unknown\) constraint`s @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : see `^*• God had reason \(yet unknown\) to make the safehold` @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            : see `^*• cosmocrafters have reason \(yet unknown\) to.+craft`s @
              ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            - therefore none quite explains the safehold, let alone the coincidence it partakes in
    - yet reason also takes part, and some of the explanatia can be determined by the part that it takes
        - these are the artificial, design explanantia
        - there are two of them

            • supernatural design by God
                : re `^*• (.+ design) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            • mundane design by cosmic creators
                : re `^*• (.+ design) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec

        (7b) the mind of a creative designer (as figures in the two design explanantia) can both
          conform to practical-rational ground direction and (within range of its competence)
          mediate the causation of things (artifacts) as effects of that conformance
        (8b) competent cosmic designers/creators are given in both design explanantia

        : see `^*\(7b\)`
        : see `^*\(8b\)` : ∴ (9b)
       ────────────────
        (9b) the creatable artifacts of (7b) would (in the case of a design explanans)
          include artifacts of cosmic structure such as the safehold

        : see `^*\(7b\)`
        : see `^*\(9b\)` : ∴ (10b)
       ────────────────
        (10b) the explanans of supernatural design might be determined by a stable ground
          (unknown to us, but known to God) that {makes prudent}|entails our long-term survival

        : see `^*\(1\)` @ ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
        : see `^*\(7b\)`
        : see `^*\(9b\)` : ∴ (11b)
       ────────────────
        (11b) the explanans of mundane design might be determined either by the default ground,
          or by a stable ground (unknown to us, but known to the designers) that {makes prudent}|entails
          the long-term survival of mind-bearing populations

        : see `^*\(10b\)`
        : see `^*\(11b\)` : ∴ (12b)
       ────────────────
        (12b) it is clear how each design explanans might be determined such that it explains
          both the safehold (6) and the coincidence (7) in which it takes part
            : re `(safehold) (\(6\))` see `^*${2} a ${1}` @ ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
            : re `(coincide)nce (\(7\))` see `^*${2} three objects.+${1}` @
              ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
            !! overreach: only in the case of mundane design on a default ground is (7) clearly explained
                - this overreach later left me stranded, out on a limb
                    : see `^*\? how then get reason’s perdurance, the fact/actuality of it\?$` @
                      67.principle.notes_boneyard.brec
                + widen and deepen the premise, widen and weaken the conclusion
                    : see notepad:2026-10-12a : on weakening the conclusion of credibility
                      to one of promise
                    + widen the conclusion to include the explanans of natural cosmogonal selection
                    - widening the premise of coincidence by inclusion of natural selection,
                      deepening the surprise and wonder
                    + further widen and deepen these by the addition of a further threefold coincidence,
                      that among:
                        I. the sources of the three coinciding objects, namely:
                            i) reason
                            ii) natural selection
                            iii) the cosmic creator
                            : re `(three) (coincid)ing (objects)`
                              see `^*\(7\) ${1} ${3}.+${2}e` @ ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
                        II. the end/object directors that figure among the most promising of explanantia
                           for both the safehold and the threefold coincidence of objects, namely:
                            i) reason
                            ii) natural cosmogonal selection
                            iii) the cosmic creators/designers, both supernatural and mundane
                            : re `(three)fold (coincide)nce of (objects)`
                              see `^*\(7\) ${1} ${3}.+${2}` @ ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
                        III. the alternative sources of normativity at contention in the field of ethics,
                           namely:
                            i) reason
                            ii) a natural telos
                            iii) God
                        : re `a further (three)fold (coincide)nce`
                          cf. `^*\(7\) ${1} objects.+${2}` @ ../20.a_surprising_coincidence.brec
    - the same does not apply to the other non-null explanantia
        - these are the natural explanantia
        - there are three of them

            • physical necessity entailing a safehold
                : re `• (physical necessity) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            • cosmogonal path selection tending toward safeholding
                : re `• (.+) path (s.+?) .+` see `^^na.+${1} ${2}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
            • multiverse ensemble constrained toward safeholding
                : re `• (.+) (constrained) .+` see `^^${2} ${1}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec

        (13b) it is unclear how any of the natural explanantia might be determined to include a mechanism
          or process, aside from mind as it figures in the design explanantia, that does the same work
            : re `the same work`
              see `^*\(12b\).+explains both the safehold.+and the coincidence.+in which it takes part`p

        : see `^*\(12b\)`
        : see `^*\(13b\)` : ∴ (14b)
       ────────────────
        (14b) a design explanans is credible, and only a design explanans
            : ad `a design explanans` :
              supernatural ⊻ mundane, that is, the exclusivity of the disjunction
              owing to each excluding the other in its claim of safehold creation
            : ad `credible` : credence would be justified
            : ad `credible` : which of the two to credit, however, remains unclear
